# Go
bin/
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# Editor-local: go.mod sits in backend/, so an editor opened at the repository
# root has no module to anchor on and gopls falls back to a GOPATH view. A
# go.work listing both modules fixes that. It stays untracked because CI builds
# backend/ standalone on purpose — see the GOWORK note in the Makefile.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Node
node_modules/
# Vite's production output and its dependency pre-bundling cache.
dist/
.vite/
*.local
# frontend/tsconfig.json is a solution file, which makes `tsc -b` a natural
# thing to run there; it drops one of these per referenced project.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Exported diagrams. `make diagrams` regenerates them; committing them would
# add a class of file that can silently go stale against the document it came
# from.
docs/diagrams/*.svg
docs/diagrams/*.md
!docs/diagrams/INDEX.md

# Env & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!testdata/**/*.pem

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Generated from contracts/ — see contracts/codegen.mk
#
# The contents rather than the directory, so that doc.go can be excepted below:
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. doc.go is the
# one hand-written file here and its own comment says why.
backend/internal/core/generated/*
!backend/internal/core/generated/doc.go
frontend/src/protocol/generated/

# Generated by mockery — see backend/.mockery.yml. Same rule as the types
# above: regenerated by `make check`, so a stale copy cannot be committed and
# reviewed. The name is reserved for the generator; a hand-written mocks_test.go
# would be invisible to git.
backend/**/mocks_test.go

# Scratch files from `make generate-verify`
.generate-verify.*

# The tree `make setup-verify` copies the tracked files into. The target removes
# it; this entry is for the run that failed and left it, which is a 540-file copy
# of the whole tracked tree — and an un-ignored copy of the repository inside the
# repository is what the next `git add -A` commits.
#
# It used to say this mattered because `make generate-verify` would read a
# leftover as generation having touched the tree. That is not a failure this can
# have (issue #334): generate-verify diffs `git status --porcelain` from before
# generation against after, git collapses an untracked directory to a single
# `?? .setup-verify/`, and that line is in both snapshots. For the diff to see it
# the directory would have to be created *between* them, and the only thing
# running in that window is `make generate` twice.
.setup-verify/

# Claude implementation plans. The spec is a repository artefact — it records
# decisions the code has to honour. A plan is scaffolding for producing the
# code and stops being true the moment the work lands, so it stays on disk and
# out of git.
docs/plans/

# The rendered documentation site. `mkdocs build` regenerates it from docs/,
# and CI publishes it to GitHub Pages — committing the output would put a
# second, staler copy of every document in the repository.
site/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, task briefs, review packages.
.superpowers/

# Worktrees created by background agents. Ephemeral, and each one is its own
# git repository — committing them would nest a checkout inside the checkout.
.claude/worktrees/
